 { Now let's examine the same position with Black to move. } 1... { -KEY- } Kd7 $1 { Applying the distant opposition. } ( { In contrast, after } 1... Kd5 $2 2. Kc3 $1 { White gains the opposition on the next move since the black king has neither c5 nor c7 at his disposal; e.g. } Kd6 3. Kd4 Kc6 4. Ke5 { and we are back in the previous example. } ) 
