2. Kd3 $1 { Keeping the distant opposition. } ( { Evidently, both } 2. Kd4 $2 Kd6 ) 
 ( { and } 2. Ke4 $2 Kc6 { would destroy the draw. } ) 
Kc7 3. Kc3 Kb7 4. Kd3 ( { The distant opposition was no longer feasible } 4. Kb3 $2 g4 { , so White stays on a light square while awaiting Black's next move. } ) 
Ka6 5. Kc4 $1 { Diagonal opposition. } Ka7 6. Kc3 Kb7 7. Kd3 Kb6 8. Kd4 Kc7 ( { As we already have seen, } 8... Kb5 9. Kd5 Kb6 10. Kd4 { is also drawn. } ) 
9. Kc3 Kb6 10. Kd4 Ka5 11. Kc5 Ka6 12. Kc4 
