 { In this bishop ending White's space advantage and the fact that the enemy kingside pawns are placed on the 'wrong' colour made the win possible. } 1. { -KEY- } Kc5 Kc7 2. Kb5 Bd5 ( { The subtle sequence } 2... Ba2 $1 3. Kxa5 Bd5 $1 { (preventing Kb5-c5) } 4. Kb4 Kb6 $1 { (in the same spirit; instead, } Bxc6 $2 5. Bb3 { is similar to the game) would have kept Black within the drawing zone, as observed by Alejandro Botta. Certainly not an intuitive choice for most humans, and I don't think that even an experienced GM like Suba could be blamed for missing this over the board. After } 5. Kc3 ( 4... Bd5 4. Bb3 Kxc6 6. Bc4 Be6 $1 { is a key detail, improving the pawn structure before handing over the opposition to White in the pawn endgame. } ) 
Be6 6. Kd4 Ba2 7. Bd1 { (or } 7. e6 $5 Bxe6 8. Ke5 Kc7 $1 { preventing 9.Kd6, when White seems unable to progress.) } Kxc6 8. Bf3 { , Black has } Kc7 $1 { , getting ready to take the opposition after } 9. Bd5 Bxd5 10. Kxd5 Kd7 { , something which they won't achieve in the game. } ) 
3. Kxa5 Bxc6 ( { After } 3... Be4 4. Bb3 ) 
 ( { or } 3... Be6 4. Kb5 Bd5 5. Kc5 Be6 6. Bd1 $1 { followed by Bf3-d5, White also wins comfortably. } ) 
4. Bb3 $1 Be8 5. Bd5 $1 { Zugzwang, or diagonal opposition, name it as you like. } Kd8 6. Kb6 Ke7 7. Bc6 $1 { A well-calculated transposition to a pawn ending. } Bxc6 ( { After } 7... Bd7 8. Bxd7 Kxd7 9. Kb7 ) 
 ( { or } 7... Kd8 8. Bxe8 Kxe8 9. Kc6 { White takes the opposition even earlier. } ) 
8. Kxc6 Ke6 9. Kc5 { Triangulating without letting Black play ...Kd5. By the way, without the e5- and f7-pawns this would be a draw, similar toExample 20 (Potkin-Grischuk) had White played the correct 1.b5. } Ke7 10. Kb6 $1 Kd8 ( { The game actually went } 10... Kd7 11. Kb7 { and Black resigned. } ) 
11. Kc6 { Black can no longer take the 'side' opposition by ...Ke6, and has to let the enemy king enter. } Ke8 12. Kd6 Kf8 ( { On } 12... Kd8 { there follows the same thing. } ) 
13. e6 ( { White wins; e.g. } 13. e6 fxe6 14. Kxe6 Kg7 15. Ke7 Kg8 16. Kf6 Kh7 17. Kf7 ) 

